    'register' => 'B2B German addresses the reader with the formal Sie in every slot: body copy, headings, ALL-CAPS bands, form labels, placeholders, alt and aria text, the <title>, the meta description, og: tags and JSON-LD. Sie, Ihr, Ihre, Ihnen are capitalised when they address the reader; no du or ihr form appears anywhere, at any length, including short CTAs and metadata. All nouns are capitalised, compounds are one word, and a multi-word proper name inside a compound is hyphenated through (Ascential-Care-Team, Ascentialytics-Plattform). Avoid Anglicisms where a settled German trade term exists; universal tech words stay (Software, Cloud, Dashboard). BUTTONS AND LINK LABELS follow German web-UI convention: they keep the verb of the English and take the bare infinitive or a noun phrase — never a du-imperative, never a conjugated sentence, never a possessive. „Browse catalog“ is „Katalog durchsuchen“, „Download“ is „Herunterladen“, „Request a demo“ is „Demo vereinbaren“, „Log in to Ascentialytics“ is „Bei Ascentialytics anmelden“. Never flatten a verb label into a bare noun („Katalog“, „Download“, „Demo-Anfrage“ are wrong for those). A status label or placeholder is never a command: „Searching ascentialtech.com“ is „ascentialtech.com durchsuchen“. One frame per set of sibling controls. Prose, headings, questions and metadata address the reader only as Sie („Kontaktieren Sie uns“).',
